      "snippet": "[Letterboxd Review of \"Sinners\"] It must have felt like déjà vu for Anne-Marie Duff. Having filmed Peter Mullan's excellent The Magdalene Sisters in the summer of 2001, she was back in the notorious Irish laundries for 'fallen women' in the winter of that year to shoot Sinners, a BBC film from director Aisling Walsh and writer Lizzie Mickery. Sinners is just as bleak and harrowing as Mullan's cinematic story of the Magdalen laundries. Duff stars as innocent rural girl Anne Marie, who is shipped off to the nuns when she is discovered to be pregnant out of wedlock. Shorn of hair and kitted out in a regulation smock, she is robb",
